# Discord patch notes

Until the user explicitly says to ship, draft patch notes in chat or wiki as pending. Do not post Discord "this is live" notes.

Whenever Bonesaw, Living Gear, or playerbots features actually ship, include a short Discord-ready patch notes bullet list in the reply.

- Player-facing only: no file paths, no spell IDs unless a player needs them
- ASCII-friendly plain `-` bullets, grouped by theme
- Title: `Bonesaw X.Y.Z - patch notes` from `tools/client-update/Bonesaw.version` after bumping it for this ship
- Bump `Bonesaw.version` on every ship, including server-only, so launcher and Discord stay aligned. Do not skip numbers.
- List only what is actually in worldserver or the client; omit in-progress work
- End every ship's notes with a `**Please test these things**` section just before the update line: 1-4 player-facing asks about this ship's own changes, then the longest-waiting open `status:awaiting-retest` issues (fetch with `python tools/retest_list.py --raw`; rephrase, no issue numbers in Discord), roughly 8 bullets max
- Include a short "Needs testing" section at the end asking players to check the
  reports awaiting retest. Query the live queue at notes-writing time:
  `docker exec ac-database mysql -uroot -ppassword -h127.0.0.1 acore_characters
  -e "SELECT id, description FROM lg_bug_report WHERE status IN ('attempted','open','fixed') ORDER BY id;"`
  (status='fixed' rows only belong here if they were never retest-confirmed —
  use the sweep notes from the session that fixed them). "fixed" ships that
  were closed with a retest confirmation are NOT re-listed. Pick the handful
  that map to a recent ship, phrase each as a short player-facing ask ("Try
  X, tell us if Y still happens"), no issue numbers or spell IDs. Keep the
  section under 5 bullets so it doesn't crowd the changelog; if nothing is
  genuinely awaiting player retest, omit the section entirely.
- Bold sparingly if Discord-flavored markdown helps
- Keep it simple and paste-ready for their Discord channel
- Extra jump is disabled; do not advertise it
- Append durable learnings to `A:\obsidian\jeremy\wiki\Bonesaw.md` (crashes, UI, deploy, spell IDs); ASCII-only client strings
